 introducing a transactional cache for trading data, significantly reducing database load and latency under high transaction volume.\\nMentored and managed a team of developers, improving delivery speed and overall team productivity through better code review practices and agile coordination.\\n\\nSenior Software Developer | FitechSource Saint Petersburg Ltd.\\nNov 2003 – Apr 2019\\nDeveloped trading systems for the Japanese financial market, including CFD and blockchain integration (BTC, ETH), ensuring low latency and high transaction reliability.\\nBuilt a prototype in-memory database (H2 → Oracle replication) that boosted data access speed while maintaining full persistence and consistency.\\nBuilt a cached JDBC driver wrapper enabling seamless integration into existing Java systems, reducing database load and data access time.\\nDeveloped reusable enterprise Java services as part of xTier middleware, reducing development time and code duplication for multiple internal applications.\\n\\nSoftware Engineer | Borland Software AG / Togethersoft Labs Inc, St. Petersburg\\nJan 2001 – Sep 2003\\nImplemented UML-to-XML import/export using XMI standards, enabling seamless model interoperability for JBuilder and Together IDE.\\n\\nQA Engineer/Software Developer| ZAO Comita, St. Petersburg\\nAug 1999 – Dec 2000\\nImproved QA process by automating testing for banking and supervisory systems.\\n\\nEducation\\nM.Sc., Microcomputer & Network Software – St. Petersburg Technical State University, Russia (1999)\\n\\nTechnical Skills\\nLanguages & Frameworks: Java, C#, VBA, Go, Spring, SpringBoot, Maven, Gradle, Servlets, XML, Python\\nDatabases: MySQL, Oracle, PostrgeSQL, HSQL, Redis, JDBC, NoSql Systems & Platforms: Tomcat , JBoss, WebLogic, Rabbit MQ, Kafka, AWS\\nTools: Git, BitBucket, Jenkins, Junit, IDEA, Eclipse, Redmine, Jira, Confluence, CI/CD, Grafana, DataDog, Docker, Kubernetes\\nFinance & Blockchain: Blockchain (BTC, ETH), Forex, FIX\\nEmerging Tools: AI-assisted codi