nd maintaining reliability under production constraints.\\n- Improved system maintainability by raising test coverage by 20% and streamlining documentation, reducing onboarding time for new engineers.\\n- Boosted team productivity by integrating Generative AI tools (ChatGPT, Cursor AI) into daily workflows for prototyping and troubleshooting.\\n\\nVP / Director of Software Development / Lead Software Developer | CardinalChain Software Inc, Vancouver\\nApr 2019 – Nov 2024\\n- Directed engineering and product development for enterprise-scale crypto trading platforms serving 1M+ users, ensuring reliability and operating under regulatory constraints.\\n- Introduced a transactional cache for trading data to reduce database load and latency under high transaction volume.\\n- Mentored and managed a team of developers, using code review practices and agile coordination to improve delivery execution and quality.\\n\\nSenior Software Developer | FitechSource Saint Petersburg Ltd.\\nNov 2003 – Apr 2019\\n- Developed trading systems for the Japanese financial market, including CFD and blockchain integration (BTC, ETH), with a focus on low latency and high transaction reliability.\\n- Built a prototype in-memory database (H2 → Oracle replication) to improve data access speed while maintaining persistence and consistency.\\n- Built a cached JDBC driver wrapper enabling integration into existing Java systems and reducing database load.\\n- Developed reusable enterprise Java services as part of xTier middleware to reduce code duplication across internal applications.\\n\\nSoftware Engineer | Borland Software AG / Togethersoft Labs Inc, St.\\nPetersburg\\nJan 2001 – Sep 2003\\n- Implemented UML-to-XML import/export using XMI standards, enabling model interoperability for JBuilder and Together IDE.\\n\\nQA Engineer/Software Developer| ZAO Comita, St. Petersburg\\nAug 1999 – Dec 2000\\n- Improved QA process by automating testing for banking and supervisory systems.\\n\\nEducation\\nM.Sc., Microcomputer & Network Software – St. Petersburg Technical State University, Russia (1999)\\n\\nTechnical Skills\\nLanguages: Java, C#, Python, TypeScript, VBA, Go\\nFrameworks & Build: Spring, SpringBoot, Maven, Gradle, Servlets, XML\\nDatabases & Caching: MySQL, PostgreSQL, Oracle, Redis, JDBC, HSQL, NoSql\\nMessaging & Integration: Rabbit MQ, Kafka, Message queues, Event-driven architecture, Idempotent processing, Retry-safe design\\nCloud & DevOps: AWS, Docker, Kubernetes, CI/CD, Jenkins\\nObservability: Grafana, DataDog\\nTools: Git, BitBucket, Junit, IDEA, Eclipse, Redmine, Jira, Confluence\\nSecurity/Auth Patterns: Encrypted signed session tokens, Distributed session validation via Redis, API-level access control (RBAC-style)\\nDomain: Forex, FIX, Blockchain (BTC, ETH)\\nAI-assisted development: ChatGPT, Claude, Cursor AI, OpenAI API\\nOther: Leadership and management, code-review, documentation, incident response, high performance fault tolerant distributed systems\\n\\nAdditional\\nEligible to work remotely for U.S. companies from Canada (no visa required for remote).\\n"}	{"text": "Leonid Verman\\nVancouver, BC, Canada · +1 (778) 317-3248 · leonidverman@gmail.com\\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/leonid-verman-3569b71b2/\\nMarch 15, 2026\\n\\nDear Hiring Manager,\\n\\nI am applying for the Engineering Manager, Apps & Solutions (Western Canada) role at League. I bring 15+ years of backend engineering experience and hands-on engineering leadership, including leading teams up to 15–20 engineers and delivering customer-facing roadmaps on shared timelines in regulated, high-availability environments.\\n\\nMost recently, I led a backend team at GMO-Z.com Fintech CA delivering a trading system serving 1M+ clients, where I combined sprint execution and code review discipline with quality investments—raising test coverage by 20% and improving documentation to reduce onboarding time. Previously, as VP/Director/Lead Software Developer at CardinalChain Software, I directed engineering for enterprise-scale crypto trading platforms serving 1M+ users and introduced a transactional cache to reduce database load and latency under high transaction volume.\\n\\nLeague’s Apps & Solutions model—delivering complex customer solutions while coordinating dependencies, communicating risks, and balancing “now vs later” engineering investments—matches how I’ve operated as a delivery-focused technical leader. I’m also comfortable working with security-minded constraints: I’ve built systems using patterns like encrypted signed session tokens and distributed session validation via Redis, and I’m used to pushing back on risky changes that could threaten production stability.\\n\\nI would welcome the opportunity to bring this delivery and leadership experience to League’s customer-facing engineering teams and help ship high-quality applications on tight timelines. Thank you for your time and consideration.\\n\\nSincerely,\\nLeonid Verman\\n"}	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-03-15 00:28:22.623197+00
