a horizontal scaling of trading servers to handle high request rates while preserving low-latency execution paths.\\n- Reduced database pressure for read-heavy GET endpoints using database read replicas and traffic isolation patterns.\\n- Implemented multi-layer caching to reduce database load and stabilize latency during peak traffic.\\n- Used asynchronous messaging to decouple components and smooth bursty workloads in transaction-processing flows.\\n- Designed stateless service patterns and implemented encrypted/signed session tokens with distributed session validation via Redis to support account migration between servers without breaking auth.\\n- Improved system maintainability by raising test coverage by 20% and streamlining documentation, reducing onboarding time for new engineers.\\n- Integrated Generative AI tools (ChatGPT, Cursor AI) into daily workflows to accelerate prototyping and troubleshooting while keeping engineers accountable for correctness.\\n\\nVP / Director of Software Development / Lead Software Developer | CardinalChain Software Inc, Vancouver\\nApr 2019 – Nov 2024\\n- Directed engineering and product development for enterprise-scale crypto trading platforms serving 1M+ users, ensuring reliability and regulatory compliance.\\n- Improved throughput by 25% by introducing a transactional cache for trading data, reducing database load and latency under high transaction volume.\\n- Applied idempotent processing and retry-safe patterns in asynchronous messaging flows to support reliable execution in distributed transaction pipelines.\\n- Mentored and managed a team of developers, improving delivery speed and team productivity through code review standards and agile coordination.\\n\\nSenior Software Developer | FitechSource Saint Petersburg Ltd.\\nNov 2003 – Apr 2019\\n- Developed trading systems for the Japanese financial market, including CFD and blockchain integration (BTC, ETH), ensuring low latency and high transaction reliability.\\n- Built a prototype in-memory database (H2 → Oracle replication) to improve data access speed while maintaining persistence and consistency.\\n- Built a cached JDBC driver wrapper enabling integration into existing Java systems while reducing database load and data access time.\\n- Developed reusable enterprise Java services as part of xTier middleware to reduce code duplication across internal applications.\\n\\nSoftware Engineer | Borland Software AG / Togethersoft Labs Inc, St.\\nPetersburg\\nJan 2001 – Sep 2003\\n- Implemented UML-to-XML import/export using XMI standards, enabling model interoperability for JBuilder and Together IDE.\\n\\nQA Engineer/Software Developer| ZAO Comita, St. Petersburg\\nAug 1999 – Dec 2000\\n- Improved QA process by automating testing for banking and supervisory systems.\\n\\nEducation\\nM.Sc., Microcomputer & Network Software – St. Petersburg Technical State University, Russia (1999)\\n\\nTechnical Skills\\nLanguages & Frameworks: Java, Spring, SpringBoot, Servlets, Maven, Gradle, C#, Python, Go, VBA, XML\\nDistributed Systems & Backend: high-throughput APIs, low-latency design, fault tolerance, event-driven architecture, asynchronous messaging, idempotent processing, retry_safe_design, stateless services\\nMessaging & Streaming: Rabbit MQ, Kafka\\nDatabases & Caching: MySQL, PostgreSQL, Oracle, HSQL, Redis, JDBC, database read replicas, multi-layer caching, transactional cache\\nAuthN/AuthZ Patterns: encrypted/signed session tokens, distributed session validation via Redis, RBAC-style API access control\\nCloud & DevOps: AWS, Docker, Kubernetes, Tomcat, JBoss, WebLogic, CI/CD\\nObservability & Ops: Grafana, DataDog, metrics/logs/tracing mindset, incident response\\nTools: Git, BitBucket, Jenkins, Junit, IDEA, Eclipse, Redmine, Jira, Confluence\\nFinance & Blockchain: Forex, FIX, Blockchain (BTC, ETH)\\nEmerging Tools: AI-assisted coding (ChatGPT, Claude, Cursor AI), OpenAI API, ML concepts (Scikit-Learn, TensorFlow basics)\\nOther: Leadership and management, code-review, documentation\\n"}	{"text": "Leonid Verman\\nVancouver, BC, Canada · +1 (778) 317-3248 · leonidverman@gmail.com\\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/leonid-verman-3569b71b2/\\nMarch 11, 2026\\n\\nDear Hiring Manager,\\n\\nI am applying for the Software Development Engineer, Middle Mile Disruption Detection and Execution role at Amazon.jobs. I bring 15+ years of backend engineering experience building and operating high-throughput, low-latency distributed systems in regulated fintech/crypto environments, including platforms that scaled to 1M+ users.\\n\\nAcross my recent roles, I focused on concrete scaling and reliability mechanisms that map well to high-volume transportation services: horizontal scaling of trading servers, database read replicas for read-heavy endpoints, multi-layer caching to reduce database pressure, and asynchronous messaging to decouple components under bursty load. I also built stateless service patterns and implemented encrypted/signed session tokens with distributed session validation via Redis—useful experience for maintaining correctness and availability when traffic is high and services must remain resilient.\\n\\nIn parallel, I currently work as an Independent Contractor supporting world-leading AI labs by training and evaluating LLMs on ambiguous senior-level software engineering tasks. This keeps me hands-on with GenAI-assisted development workflows and strengthens my ability to reason about tradeoffs, failure modes, and operational constraints—skills I would apply to building disruption detection and automated execution systems that must behave predictably in real-world conditions.\\n\\nI would welcome the opportunity to contribute my distributed-systems depth, operational mindset, and mentoring approach to Amazon’s Middle Mile Transportation Technology team. Thank you for your consideration.\\n\\nSincerely,\\nLeonid Verman\\n"}	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-03-11 00:10:21.643113+00
