h-availability requirements.\\n- Deployed multi-layer caching to reduce database pressure and introduced asynchronous messaging for decoupled service integration.\\n- Integrated Generative AI tools into team workflows, accelerating prototyping and troubleshooting.\\n- Raised test coverage by 20% and improved documentation, reducing onboarding time for new engineers.\\n\\nVP / Director of Software Development / Lead Software Developer | CardinalChain Software Inc, Vancouver\\nApr 2019 – Nov 2024\\n- Directed engineering and product development for enterprise-scale crypto trading platforms with 1M+ users, ensuring reliability and compliance in regulated environments.\\n- Improved system throughput by 25% through a transactional cache for trading data, reducing database load and latency during peak transaction periods.\\n- Established delivery governance practices, including release cadence and escalation frameworks, to improve predictability and risk management.\\n- Mentored and managed teams up to 20 engineers, implementing code review standards and continuous improvement processes.\\n- Set architectural direction for distributed session validation via Redis and stateless service design to support account migration and high-throughput validation.\\n\\nSenior Software Developer | FitechSource Saint Petersburg Ltd.\\nNov 2003 – Apr 2019\\n- Developed low-latency trading systems for the Japanese financial market, including blockchain integration (BTC, ETH).\\n- Built a prototype in-memory database (H2 → Oracle replication) to accelerate data access while maintaining consistency.\\n- Designed a cached JDBC driver wrapper for integration boundaries, reducing database load and improving access times.\\n- Delivered reusable enterprise Java services as part of a modular backend component strategy, reducing code duplication.\\n\\nSoftware Engineer | Borland Software AG / Togethersoft Labs Inc, St. Petersburg\\nJan 2001 – Sep 2003\\n- Implemented UML-to-XML import/export using