tomating testing for banking and supervisory systems.\\n\\nEducation\\nM.Sc., Microcomputer & Network Software – St. Petersburg Technical State University, Russia (1999)\\n\\nTechnical Skills\\nLanguages & Frameworks: Java, Spring, SpringBoot, Servlets, Maven, Gradle, C#, Go, Python, VBA, XML\\nAPI & Integration: REST, JDBC\\nDatabases & Caching: PostgreSQL, MySQL, Oracle, HSQL, Redis\\nMessaging & Streaming: Rabbit MQ, Kafka\\nCloud & Platforms: AWS, Tomcat, JBoss, WebLogic, Docker, Kubernetes\\nObservability & DevOps: Jenkins, CI/CD, Grafana, DataDog\\nTools: Git, BitBucket, Junit, IDEA, Eclipse, Redmine, Jira, Confluence\\nFinance & Blockchain: Forex, FIX, Blockchain (BTC, ETH)\\nEmerging Tools: AI-assisted coding (ChatGPT, Claude, Cursor AI), ML concepts (Scikit-Learn, TensorFlow basics)\\nOther: high performance fault tolerant distributed systems, stateless service design, asynchronous messaging, database read replicas, multi-layer caching, distributed session validation via Redis, idempotent processing and retry-safe patterns, transactional cache, code-review, documentation, leadership and management\\n"}	{"text": "Leonid Verman\\nVancouver, BC, Canada · +1 (778) 317-3248 · leonidverman@gmail.com\\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/leonid-verman-3569b71b2/\\nMarch 11, 2026\\n\\nDear Hiring Manager,\\n\\nI am applying for the Lead Software Engineer (Java & GraphQL) role at Kubikware. I bring 15+ years of backend engineering experience in high-throughput fintech and crypto systems, including hands-on leadership as VP/Director and team lead, delivering production platforms at 1M+ user scale under reliability and regulatory constraints.\\n\\nAcross my recent roles, I focused on API-driven backend services where performance and scalability were first-class requirements. I have implemented concrete scaling mechanisms such as horizontal scaling of trading servers, stateless service design with distributed session validation via Redis, database read replicas for read-heavy 