rove data access speed while maintaining persistence and consistency.\\n- Built a cached JDBC driver wrapper to integrate into existing Java systems and reduce database load and data access time.\\n- Developed reusable enterprise Java services as part of xTier middleware to reduce development time and code duplication across internal applications.\\n\\nSoftware Engineer | Borland Software AG / Togethersoft Labs Inc, St.\\nPetersburg\\nJan 2001 – Sep 2003\\n- Implemented UML-to-XML import/export using XMI standards to enable model interoperability for JBuilder and Together IDE.\\n\\nQA Engineer/Software Developer| ZAO Comita, St. Petersburg\\nAug 1999 – Dec 2000\\n- Improved QA process by automating testing for banking and supervisory systems.\\n\\nEducation\\nM.Sc., Microcomputer & Network Software – St. Petersburg Technical State University, Russia (1999)\\n\\nTechnical Skills\\nLanguages & Frameworks: Java, Spring, SpringBoot, Servlets, Maven, Gradle, Python, C#, TypeScript, XML, VBA\\nAPI & Integration: REST, WebSockets, JDBC\\nDatabases & Caching: PostgreSQL, MySQL, Oracle, Redis, HSQL\\nMessaging & Event-Driven: Kafka, Rabbit MQ, Message queues, Idempotent processing, Retry-safe design\\nCloud & DevOps: AWS, Docker, Kubernetes, Tomcat, JBoss, WebLogic, CI/CD, Jenkins\\nObservability & Ops: Grafana, DataDog, Metrics/logs/tracing mindset\\nTools: Git, BitBucket, Junit, IDEA, Eclipse, Redmine, Jira, Confluence\\nFinance & Blockchain: Blockchain (BTC, ETH), Forex, FIX\\nEmerging Tools: AI-assisted coding (ChatGPT, Claude, Cursor AI), OpenAI API, ML concepts (Scikit-Learn, TensorFlow basics)\\nOther: Leadership and management, high performance fault tolerant distributed systems, code-review, documentation\\n"}	{"text": "Leonid Verman\\nVancouver, BC, Canada · +1 (778) 317-3248 · leonidverman@gmail.com\\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/leonid-verman-3569b71b2/\\nMarch 12, 2026\\n\\nDear Hiring Manager,\\n\\nI’m applying for the Lead Software Engineer (Java & GraphQL) rol