610e6b6c-69ff-4e90-9064-3efce8870c9c	fe1493e3-80d2-4396-8138-c586c9ecef81	ac0bd62b-7a52-4d55-ad3b-0c8a4184189c	CARFAX	Senior Software Engineer - Team Lead	{"text": "Oli Treadwell\\nolitreadwell@gmail.com | +64 22 451 9939 (Text first please)\\nlinkedin.com/in/olitreadwell | github.com/olitreadwell | Book a Call\\nSenior Software Engineer\\n\\nSUMMARY\\nSenior Software Engineer with 10+ years of experience building modern web applications with React and TypeScript across customer-facing and internal workflow products. Strengths include front-end architecture (component libraries, design systems, Rails-to-React migrations), full-stack delivery with Node.js/Rails and relational databases, and disciplined testing/CI practices. Known for accessible, user-friendly UI implementation and collaborative delivery with product and design partners.\\n\\nSKILLS\\n- Frontend & UX: React, TypeScript, Next.js, Storybook, CSS/SCSS, Design systems, Localisation\\n- Backend & APIs: Node.js, .NET, Ruby on Rails, Python Flask, GraphQL, REST/JSON:API, Schema design\\n- DevOps & Tooling: AWS, Docker, GitHub Actions, CircleCI, Cypress, Jest/React Testing Library (RTL), Monitoring\\n- Leadership & Accessibility: Technical mentoring, Stakeholder facilitation, Accessibility advocacy\\n\\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\\nSenior Software Engineer | Numeral Studio | Wellington, NZ | 2025 – Present\\n- Built React/TypeScript interfaces and Prisma-backed Node/Express services for HR case workflows, including dynamic staff routing and permissions-sensitive UI behavior.\\n- Delivered reusable React/TypeScript components inside Electron with accessible, responsive UI patterns plus Jest/React Testing Library coverage to reduce manual errors in compliance reporting workflows.\\n- Supported the launch of the design conference 2025 and 2026 site on Next.js/TypeScript with Sanity CMS and Storybook, extending the design system to reduce duplicate UI code.\\n- Added automated ESLint/Prettier and unit-test checks in CI (GitHub Actions) to keep day-to-day delivery consistent across contributors.\\n- Contributed localized feature work for a mobile-first progressive web app marketing demo, coordinating with remote teammates and tuning performance for global launches.\\n- Technologies: React, Next.js, Electron, TypeScript, SCSS, Node.js/Express, Prisma ORM, Sanity CMS, Storybook, GSAP, Cypress, Jest, React Testing Library, GitHub Actions, ESLint, Prettier, localization & accessibility tools.\\n\\nSoftware Engineer (Contract) | PartsTrader Markets Ltd. | Wellington, NZ | 2024 – 2025\\n- Developed a dedicated .NET microservice to interface with a legacy API and built a modern, responsive front-end using React with TypeScript.\\n- Translated Figma UI designs into dynamic, accessible interfaces using React, TypeScript, and styled-components.\\n- Applied Domain-Driven Design by structuring the microservice with Repository, Domain Model, Mapper, and Application Service patterns.\\n- Technologies: .NET service layer, React, TypeScript, Cypress, GitHub Actions, domain-driven design patterns.\\n\\nSoftware Engineer & Founder | Habitual Genesis | Remote | 2016 – Present\\n- Partner with authors, museums, and education nonprofits to ship low-maintenance digital products.\\n- Delivered discovery-through-launch engagements while keeping ongoing costs low.\\n- Embedded with stakeholders to clarify needs, prioritize MVPs, and trial marketing ideas without raising spend.\\n- Various projects with General Assembly, Thinkful, Codecademy, and others\\n- Technologies: JavaScript, HTML5, CSS3, Bootstrap, GitHub, GitHub Pages, Squarespace, Mailchimp, Google Drive.\\n\\nSoftware Engineer & Lead Instructor | The Flatiron School | Remote | 2022 – 2023\\n- Delivered remote & asynchronous technical training on software engineering to a diverse group of students.\\n- Wrote and presented curriculum covering JavaScript, HTML/CSS, ReactJS, Python, Flask, PostgreSQL, Object-Oriented Programming, CI/CD, Agile, APIs, Web Accessibility, and more.\\n- Mentored and coached junior engineers, preparing them for success in their roles and job duties.\\n- Lead a working group promoting inclusive web design and web accessibility practices.\\n- Technologies: JavaScript, HTML5, CSS3, ReactJS, React Router, Python, Flask, Object-Oriented Programming, CI/CD, Render.com, Agile, APIs, Web Accessibility\\n\\nSenior Software Engineer | WorkTango (formerly KazooHR) | Remote | 2019 – 2020\\n- Re-architected the Rewards platform from Rails to ReactJS, resulting in a 15% increase in customer engagement.\\n- Implemented a modular design system to improve UI consistency and boost developer velocity.\\n- Integrated features across Performance Management and Rewards platforms to overhaul the product suite.\\n- Technologies: ReactJS, Storybook, NodeJS, Jest, Chai, TypeScript, Ruby on Rails, ActiveRecord, RSpec, GraphQL, PostgreSQL, Circle CI, SASS/SCSS, GitHub, Design Language Systems, JIRA, Zeplin, Figma.\\n\\nSoftware Engineer | Condé Nast | Austin, TX | 2017 – 2019\\n- Delivered new design features & ReactJS components for over 26 media brands, improving readership and SEO.\\n- Built and iterated upon a brand-agnostic paywall architecture and a suite of components, driving significant growth and achieving a year-over-year increase of over 100% in monthly subscriptions for Vanity Fair and Wired.\\n- Authored a technology blog post on End-to-End Testing of the Condé Nast Paywalls. https://technology.condenast.com/story/end-to-end-testing-conde-nast-paywalls\\n- Technologies: ReactJS, Storybook, NodeJS, Jest, Puppeteer, TypeScript, SASS, GitHub, Jenkins, CI/CD, Design Language Systems, JIRA.\\n\\nSoftware Engineer & Instructor | Hack Reactor (formerly Galvanize) | Austin, TX | 2016 – 2017\\n- Facilitated technical workshops for full-time and part-time programs in an Agile environment.\\n- Built a mock interview app for students, exponentially increasing career services' capacity to give feedback.\\n- Technologies: ReactJS, JavaScript, jQuery, Mocha, Chai, HTML, CSS3, SASS/SCSS, PostgreSQL, MySQL, Git, GitHub, Heroku, bash, zsh.\\n\\nSoftware Engineer (Contract) | Bypass Mobile | Austin, TX | 2016 – 2016\\n- Designed and developed a JSON-API spec product licensing platform using Ruby on Rails as part of a small team.\\n- Technologies: JSON-API, Ruby on Rails, ActiveRecord, RSpec, MySQL, Git, GitHub, Vagrant, bash, JIRA.\\n\\nSoftware Engineer | Union Metrics | Austin, TX | 2014 – 2016\\n- Migrated and refactored two legacy codebases to use Rails 4, improving maintainability, security of core business features, and performance by 20%.\\n- Created a knowledge base of 100 most common customer technical challenges, reducing resolution time by 50%.\\n- Technologies: JavaScript, Ruby on Rails, ActiveRecord, RSpec, jQuery, HTML, CSS3, SASS/SCSS, MySQL, Git, GitHub, Vagrant, Jenkins, bash.\\n\\nEDUCATION\\nPostgraduate Diploma in Information Technology | Whitireia and WelTec, New Zealand\\nFull-Stack Web Development, Ruby on Rails, and JavaScript Certification | Dev Bootcamp\\nBS in Business Administration, Entrepreneurship, & International Business | Chapman University\\n\\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\\nFor more details, you can find answers to common hiring questions, my references, and a detailed list of my skills and experience at the following links:\\n- Common Hiring Questions: github.com/olitreadwell/resume/blob/main/common-hiring-questions.md\\n- Portfolio Projects: https://github.com/olitreadwell/resume/blob/main/portfolio-projects.md\\n- Professional References: github.com/olitreadwell/resume/blob/main/linkedin-recommendations.md\\n- Skills and Experience: github.com/olitreadwell/resume/blob/main/skills-and-experience.md"}	{"text": "Oli Treadwell\\nolitreadwell@gmail.com | +64 22 451 9939 | linkedin.com/in/olitreadwell\\nMarch 16, 2026\\n\\nDear Hiring Manager,\\n\\nI’m applying for the Senior Software Engineer – Team Lead role at CARFAX. I’m a Senior Software Engineer with 10+ years of experience building modern web applications, with a focus on React/TypeScript UI architecture, component-driven development, and full-stack delivery with Node.js/Rails and relational databases.\\n\\nIn recent roles, I’ve delivered reusable React/TypeScript component libraries and design-system work (Storybook) to keep UI consistent across products, and I’ve paired that with disciplined testing and CI practices (Jest/React Testing Library, Cypress, GitHub Actions/CircleCI). At WorkTango, I re-architected a Rewards platform from Rails to ReactJS, which corresponded with a 15% increase in customer engagement. At Numeral Studio, I built React/TypeScript interfaces and Node/Express services for HR case workflows, including permissions-sensitive behavior and automated lint/test checks to keep delivery predictable.\\n\\nCARFAX’s focus on high-use customer-facing experiences and quality engineering practices is a strong match for how I work day-to-day: collaborating closely with product and design partners, documenting and standardizing UI patterns, and raising the bar on maintainability through shared components and tests. While my background is primarily web product engineering (rather than dedicated authentication specialization), I’ve repeatedly worked in areas where correctness, permissions, and consistent user experience matter.\\n\\nI’d welcome the opportunity to discuss how my front-end architecture and full-stack delivery experience can support CARFAX’s Account Engineering team.\\n\\nSincerely,\\nOli Treadwell"}	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-03-16 01:31:36.411736+00
