atterns consistent.\\n- Contributed localized feature work for a mobile-first interactive marketing demo (progressive web app), collaborating with remote teams and tuning performance for fast global launches.\\n- Technologies: React, Next.js, Electron, TypeScript, SCSS, Node.js/Express, Prisma ORM, Sanity CMS, Storybook, GSAP, Cypress, Jest, React Testing Library, GitHub Actions, ESLint, Prettier, localization & accessibility tools.\\n\\nSoftware Engineer (Contract) | PartsTrader Markets Ltd. | Wellington, NZ | 2024 – 2025\\n- Developed a dedicated .NET microservice to interface with a legacy API and built a modern, responsive front-end using React with TypeScript.\\n- Translated Figma UI designs into dynamic, accessible interfaces using React, TypeScript, and styled-components.\\n- Applied Domain-Driven Design principles by structuring the microservice with Repository, Domain Model, Mapper, and Application Service patterns.\\n- Technologies: .NET service layer, React, TypeScript, Cypress, GitHub Actions, domain-driven design patterns.\\n\\nSoftware Engineer & Founder | Habitual Genesis | Remote | 2016 – Present\\n- Partner with authors, museums, and education nonprofits to ship low-maintenance digital products.\\n- Delivered discovery-through-launch engagements while keeping ongoing costs low.\\n- Embedded with stakeholders to clarify needs, prioritize MVPs, and trial marketing ideas without raising spend.\\n- Various projects with General Assembly, Thinkful, Codecademy, and others.\\n- Technologies: JavaScript, HTML5, CSS3, Bootstrap, GitHub, GitHub Pages, Squarespace, Mailchimp, Google Drive.\\n\\nSoftware Engineer & Lead Instructor | The Flatiron School | Remote | 2022 – 2023\\n- Delivered remote & asynchronous technical training on software engineering to a diverse group of students.\\n- Wrote and presented curriculum covering JavaScript, HTML/CSS, ReactJS, Python, Flask, PostgreSQL, Object-Oriented Programming, CI/CD, Agile, APIs, and Web Accessibility.\\n- Mentored and coached junior engineers, preparing them for success in their roles and job duties.\\n- Led a working group promoting inclusive web design and web accessibility practices.\\n- Technologies: JavaScript, HTML5, CSS3, ReactJS, React Router, Python, Flask, Object-Oriented Programming, CI/CD, Render.com, Agile, APIs, Web Accessibility.\\n\\nSenior Software Engineer | WorkTango (formerly KazooHR) | Remote | 2019 – 2020\\n- Re-architected the Rewards platform UI from Rails-rendered views to ReactJS, resulting in a 15% increase in customer engagement.\\n- Implemented a modular design system to improve UI consistency and boost developer velocity.\\n- Integrated features across Performance Management and Rewards platforms to support an overhaul of the product suite.\\n- Technologies: ReactJS, Storybook, NodeJS, Jest, Chai, TypeScript, Ruby on Rails, ActiveRecord, RSpec, GraphQL, PostgreSQL, Circle CI, SASS/SCSS, GitHub, Design Language Systems, JIRA, Zeplin, Figma.\\n\\nSoftware Engineer | Condé Nast | Austin, TX | 2017 – 2019\\n- Delivered new design features and ReactJS components for over 26 media brands, improving readership and SEO.\\n- Built and iterated on a brand-agnostic paywall architecture and component suite, achieving a year-over-year increase of over 100% in monthly subscriptions for Vanity Fair and Wired.\\n- Authored a technology blog post on End-to-End Testing of the Condé Nast Paywalls: https://technology.condenast.com/story/end-to-end-testing-conde-nast-paywalls\\n- Technologies: ReactJS, Storybook, NodeJS, Jest, Puppeteer, TypeScript, SASS, GitHub, Jenkins, CI/CD, Design Language Systems, JIRA.\\n\\nSoftware Engineer & Instructor | Hack Reactor (formerly Galvanize) | Austin, TX | 2016 – 2017\\n- Facilitated technical workshops for full-time and part-time programs in an Agile environment.\\n- Built a mock interview app for students, increasing career services' capacity to give feedback.\\n- Technologies: ReactJS, JavaScript, jQuery, Mocha, Chai, HTML, CSS3, SASS/SCSS, PostgreSQL, MySQL, Git, GitHub, Heroku, bash, zsh.\\n\\nSoftware Engineer (Contract) | Bypass Mobile | Austin, TX | 2016 – 2016\\n- Designed and developed a JSON-API spec product licensing platform using Ruby on Rails as part of a small team.\\n- Technologies: JSON-API, Ruby on Rails, ActiveRecord, RSpec, MySQL, Git, GitHub, Vagrant, bash, JIRA.\\n\\nSoftware Engineer | Union Metrics | Austin, TX | 2014 – 2016\\n- Migrated and refactored two legacy codebases to use Rails 4, improving maintainability, security of core business features, and performance by 20%.\\n- Created a knowledge base of 100 most common customer technical challenges, reducing resolution time by 50%.\\n- Technologies: JavaScript, Ruby on Rails, ActiveRecord, RSpec, jQuery, HTML, CSS3, SASS/SCSS, MySQL, Git, GitHub, Vagrant, Jenkins, bash.\\n\\nEDUCATION\\nPostgraduate Diploma in Information Technology | Whitireia and WelTec, New Zealand\\nFull-Stack Web Development, Ruby on Rails, and JavaScript Certification | Dev Bootcamp\\nBS in Business Administration, Entrepreneurship, & International Business | Chapman University\\n\\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\\nFor more details, you can find answers to common hiring questions, my references, and a detailed list of my skills and experience at the following links:\\n- Common Hiring Questions: github.com/olitreadwell/resume/blob/main/common-hiring-questions.md\\n- Portfolio Projects: https://github.com/olitreadwell/resume/blob/main/portfolio-projects.md\\n- Professional References: github.com/olitreadwell/resume/blob/main/linkedin-recommendations.md\\n- Skills and Experience: github.com/olitreadwell/resume/blob/main/skills-and-experience.md\\n", "template_original_filename": "Oli Treadwell - Senior Software Engineer Resume - 2026-03-06.pdf"}	{"text": "March 18, 2026\\n\\nDear Hiring Manager,\\n\\nI’m applying for the Senior Software Engineer – Team Lead role at CARFAX. I’m a Senior Software Engineer with 10+ years building modern web applications, with deep experience in React and TypeScript UI architecture, full-stack delivery with Node.js and Ruby on Rails, and a consistent focus on accessible, user-friendly customer experiences.\\n\\nAcross product environments, I’ve modernized and standardized front-end systems to improve consistency and delivery. At WorkTango, I re-architected a Rewards platform UI from Rails-rendered views to ReactJS and helped implement a modular design system for shared UI patterns. In my current role at Numeral Studio, I deliver reusable React/TypeScript components (including Electron-based UI) with Jest/React Testing Library coverage, and I build Node/Express services that support HR case workflows with permissions hardening and automated lint/test checks.\\n\\nThe Team Lead aspect of this role is a strong fit for how I work day-to-day: leading by example, delegating ownership, and using code review and coaching to help engineers grow through technical challenges. I also take a risk-based approach to production stability—pushing back on changes that increase operational risk without clear benefit.\\n\\nI’d welcome the opportunity to bring my front-end architecture strengths, full-stack pragmatism, and hands-on mentorship to CARFAX’s Account Engineering team as you build secure, consistent login and profile experiences.\\n\\nSincerely,\\nOli Treadwell\\n"}	documents/fe1493e3-80d2-4396-8138-c586c9ecef81/generated/53e225a0-7674-4869-99a4-6843f462cd1f/resume.docx	documents/fe1493e3-80d2-4396-8138-c586c9ecef81/generated/53e225a0-7674-4869-99a4-6843f462cd1f/resume.pdf	documents/fe1493e3-80d2-4396-8138-c586c9ecef81/generated/53e225a0-7674-4869-99a4-6843f462cd1f/cover_letter.docx	documents/fe1493e3-80d2-4396-8138-c586c9ecef81/generated/53e225a0-7674-4869-99a4-6843f462cd1f/cover_letter.pdf	2026-03-18 02:33:52.653708+00
