workflows to accelerate prototyping and troubleshooting while keeping engineers accountable for output quality.\\n\\nVP / Director of Software Development / Lead Software Developer | CardinalChain Software Inc, Vancouver\\nApr 2019 – Nov 2024\\n- Directed engineering and product development for enterprise-scale crypto trading platforms serving 1M+ users, balancing delivery timelines with reliability and regulatory constraints.\\n- Improved system throughput by 25% by introducing a transactional cache for trading data to reduce database load and latency under high transaction volume.\\n- Scaled low-latency backend services via horizontal scaling of trading servers, with stateless service design to support growth and operational flexibility.\\n- Isolated read-heavy GET endpoints from write workloads using database read replicas, protecting core transactional paths under peak demand.\\n- Reduced database pressure using multiple caching layers, selecting cache boundaries appropriate for correctness-sensitive trading data.\\n- Decoupled components using asynchronous messaging to reduce tight coupling and support independent evolution of backend services.\\n- Implemented stateless authentication patterns using encrypted signed session tokens with distributed session validation via Redis, including centralized revocation and account context extraction from tokens.\\n- Supported safe account rebalancing and migration between servers without breaking authentication, aligning operational tooling with production safety needs.\\n- Mentored and managed a team of developers, using collaborative code review practices and agile coordination to improve delivery speed and consistency.\\n\\nSenior Software Developer | FitechSource Saint Petersburg Ltd.\\nNov 2003 – Apr 2019\\n- Developed trading systems for the Japanese financial market, including CFD and blockchain integration (BTC, ETH), with low-latency and high reliability requirements.\\n- Built a prototype in-memory database (H2 → Oracle replication) to improve data access speed while maintaining persistence and consistency.\\n- Built a cached JDBC driver wrapper to integrate into existing Java systems and reduce database load and data access time.\\n- Developed reusable enterprise Java services as part of xTier middleware to reduce development time and code duplication across internal applications.\\n\\nSoftware Engineer | Borland Software AG / Togethersoft Labs Inc, St.\\nPetersburg\\nJan 2001 – Sep 2003\\n- Implemented UML-to-XML import/export using XMI standards to enable model interoperability for JBuilder and Together IDE.\\n\\nQA Engineer/Software Developer| ZAO Comita, St. Petersburg\\nAug 1999 – Dec 2000\\n- Improved QA process by automating testing for banking and supervisory systems.\\n\\nEducation\\nM.Sc., Microcomputer & Network Software – St. Petersburg Technical State University, Russia (1999)\\n\\nTechnical Skills\\nLanguages & Frameworks: Java, C#, Python, TypeScript, VBA, Go, Spring, SpringBoot, Maven, Gradle, Servlets, XML\\nData & Databases: MySQL, PostgreSQL, Oracle, Redis, JDBC, HSQL, NoSql Systems\\nDistributed Systems & Messaging: Rabbit MQ, Kafka, Message queues, Idempotent processing, Retry-safe design\\nAPIs & Integration: REST, WebSockets, FIX\\nCloud & DevOps: AWS, Docker, Kubernetes, Tomcat, JBoss, WebLogic, CI/CD\\nTools: Git, BitBucket, Jenkins, Junit, IDEA, Eclipse, Redmine, Jira, Confluence, Grafana, DataDog\\nAI-assisted Delivery: AI-assisted coding (ChatGPT, Claude, Cursor AI)\\nFinance & Blockchain: Blockchain (BTC, ETH), Forex\\nOther: Leadership and management, high performance fault tolerant distributed systems, code-review, documentation\\n", "template_original_filename": "Leonid_Verman_Resume_Template.docx"}	{"text": "Leonid Verman\\nVancouver, BC, Canada · +1 (778) 317-3248 · leonidverman@gmail.com\\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/leonid-verman-3569b71b2/\\nMarch 18, 2026\\n\\nDear Hiring Manager,\\n\\nI’m applying for the Technical Product Lead role at Boam AI. My background is as a hands-on backend engineer and engineering leader (15+ years) who has repeatedly turned real customer and market constraints into shipped systems—most notably building and scaling a high-throughput transaction platform for the Japanese market to 1M+ users (top-5 by trading volume; at times #1). I’m comfortable operating close to the metal—schemas, APIs, caching layers, async messaging, and reliability guardrails—while keeping delivery sequencing and tradeoffs clear for the team.\\n\\nIn my most recent leadership role (VP/Director/Lead Software Developer), I directed engineering and product development for enterprise-scale trading platforms under regulatory and timeline constraints. That work required tight execution across backend components and data paths: isolating read-heavy endpoints via database read replicas, reducing database load with multiple caching layers, decoupling services with asynchronous messaging, and implementing stateless auth patterns with encrypted signed session tokens and Redis-backed session validation/revocation. I also led teams up to 15–20 engineers with an emphasis on crisp task definition, collaborative code review, and predictable delivery without unnecessary process.\\n\\nI also currently work as an independent contractor via Mercor supporting world-leading AI labs on LLM training and evaluation for ambiguous senior-level software engineering tasks. Separately, I’ve integrated AI tools (ChatGPT, Cursor AI; also familiar with Claude) into day-to-day engineering workflows to accelerate prototyping and troubleshooting while maintaining accountability and safe usage practices—an approach that aligns with Boam AI’s focus on using next-gen AI tools to speed discovery and execution.\\n\\nBoam AI’s mission—turning messy, unstructured signals into structured, reliable intelligence that powers CRMs, data warehouses, and mission-critical decisions—maps well to how I’ve built and operated correctness-sensitive systems: define the workflow, make tradeoffs explicit, ship incrementally, and protect quality where it matters. I’d welcome the chance to discuss how I’d drive end-to-end delivery with your CEO, data/engineering/ML teams, and enterprise customers.\\n\\nSincerely,\\nLeonid Verman\\n"}	documents/27af6204-a05d-4fc9-8115-a1df26c83ebd/generated/575fd3f1-d758-4113-9560-1a73863013ea/resume.docx	documents/27af6204-a05d-4fc9-8115-a1df26c83ebd/generated/575fd3f1-d758-4113-9560-1a73863013ea/resume.pdf	documents/27af6204-a05d-4fc9-8115-a1df26c83ebd/generated/575fd3f1-d758-4113-9560-1a73863013ea/cover_letter.docx	documents/27af6204-a05d-4fc9-8115-a1df26c83ebd/generated/575fd3f1-d758-4113-9560-1a73863013ea/cover_letter.pdf	2026-03-18 05:38:42.520546+00
