nt / Lead Software Developer | CardinalChain Software Inc, Vancouver\\nApr 2019 – Nov 2024\\n- Directed engineering and product development for enterprise-scale crypto trading platforms serving 1M+ users, operating under regulatory and delivery constraints.\\n- Improved system throughput by 25% by introducing a transactional cache for trading data to reduce database load and latency under high transaction volume.\\n- Mentored and managed a team of developers; improved delivery speed and team productivity through collaborative code review practices and agile coordination.\\n\\nSenior Software Developer | FitechSource Saint Petersburg Ltd.\\nNov 2003 – Apr 2019\\n- Developed trading systems for the Japanese financial market, including CFD and blockchain integration (BTC, ETH), with low-latency and high-reliability requirements.\\n- Built a prototype in-memory database (H2 → Oracle replication) to increase data access speed while maintaining persistence and consistency.\\n- Built a cached JDBC driver wrapper to integrate into existing Java systems and reduce database load.\\n- Developed reusable enterprise Java services as part of xTier middleware to reduce development time and code duplication across internal applications.\\n\\nSoftware Engineer | Borland Software AG / Togethersoft Labs Inc, St. Petersburg\\nJan 2001 – Sep 2003\\n- Implemented UML-to-XML import/export using XMI standards to enable model interoperability for JBuilder and Together IDE.\\n\\nQA Engineer/Software Developer | ZAO Comita, St. Petersburg\\nAug 1999 – Dec 2000\\n- Improved QA process by automating testing for banking and supervisory systems.\\n\\nEducation\\nM.Sc., Microcomputer & Network Software – St. Petersburg Technical State University, Russia (1999)\\n\\nTechnical Skills\\nLanguages & Frameworks: Java, C#, Python, TypeScript, VBA, Go, Spring, SpringBoot, Maven, Gradle, Servlets, XML\\nData & Databases: MySQL, PostgreSQL, Oracle, Redis, JDBC, HSQL, NoSql\\nDistributed Systems & Messaging