 of Software Development / Lead Software Developer | CardinalChain Software Inc, Vancouver\\nApr 2019 – Nov 2024\\n- Directed engineering and product development for enterprise-scale crypto trading platforms serving 1M+ users, balancing delivery timelines with regulatory and operational constraints.\\n- Improved system throughput by 25% by introducing a transactional cache for trading data, reducing database load and latency under high transaction volume.\\n- Mentored and managed a team of developers, improving delivery speed and team execution through code review practices and agile coordination.\\n\\nSenior Software Developer | FitechSource Saint Petersburg Ltd.\\nNov 2003 – Apr 2019\\n- Developed trading systems for the Japanese financial market, including CFD and blockchain integration (BTC, ETH), with a focus on low-latency behavior and high transaction reliability.\\n- Built a prototype in-memory database (H2 → Oracle replication) to improve data access speed while maintaining persistence and consistency.\\n- Built a cached JDBC driver wrapper enabling integration into existing Java systems while reducing database load and data access time.\\n- Developed reusable enterprise Java services as part of xTier middleware to reduce development time and code duplication across internal applications.\\n\\nSoftware Engineer | Borland Software AG / Togethersoft Labs Inc, St.\\nPetersburg\\nJan 2001 – Sep 2003\\n- Implemented UML-to-XML import/export using XMI standards to enable model interoperability for JBuilder and Together IDE.\\n\\nQA Engineer/Software Developer| ZAO Comita, St. Petersburg\\nAug 1999 – Dec 2000\\n- Improved QA process by automating testing for banking and supervisory systems.\\n\\nEducation\\nM.Sc., Microcomputer & Network Software – St. Petersburg Technical State University, Russia (1999)\\n\\nTechnical Skills\\nLanguages & Frameworks: Java, C#, Python, TypeScript, VBA, Go, Spring, SpringBoot, Maven, Gradle, Servlets, XML\\nData & Databases: MySQL, PostgreSQL, Oracle, Redis, JDBC, HSQL, NoSql\\nDistributed Systems & Messaging: Rabbit MQ, RabbitMQ, Kafka, message queues, idempotent processing, retry-safe design\\nAPIs & Integration: REST, WebSockets, FIX\\nInfra / DevOps: AWS, Docker, Kubernetes, Tomcat, JBoss, WebLogic, CI/CD\\nEngineering Tools: Git, BitBucket, Jenkins, Junit, IDEA, Eclipse, Redmine, Jira, Confluence, Grafana, DataDog\\nAI Tooling: AI-assisted coding (ChatGPT, Claude, Cursor AI)\\nFinance & Blockchain: Blockchain (BTC, ETH), Forex\\nOther: Leadership and management, high performance fault tolerant distributed systems, code-review, documentation\\n", "template_original_filename": "Leonid_Verman_Resume_Template.docx"}	{"text": "Leonid Verman\\nVancouver, BC, Canada · +1 (778) 317-3248 · leonidverman@gmail.com\\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/leonid-verman-3569b71b2/\\nMarch 18, 2026\\n\\nDear Hiring Manager,\\n\\nI’m applying for the Technical Product Lead role at Boam AI. My background combines hands-on backend engineering with delivery leadership across data- and API-heavy fintech systems, including regulated trading platforms scaled to 1M+ users. In roles spanning Lead Engineer through VP/Director, I’ve repeatedly translated real operational workflows into clear execution plans and shipped outcomes with high standards for correctness and reliability.\\n\\nAt GMO-Z.com Fintech CA, I led a backend team delivering a trading system for 1M+ clients in Japan, improving maintainability by raising test coverage by 20% and streamlining documentation to reduce onboarding time. Earlier at CardinalChain, I directed engineering and product development for crypto trading platforms serving 1M+ users and improved throughput by introducing a transactional cache to reduce database load and latency under high transaction volume—work that required tight sequencing, pragmatic tradeoffs, and consistent execution.\\n\\nI also currently work as an independent contractor supporting world-leading AI labs on LLM training and evaluation for senior software engineering tasks. This keeps me sharp on ambiguity-heavy problem framing and reinforces disciplined use of AI tools (e.g., ChatGPT, Claude, Cursor AI) to accelerate discovery and execution while keeping engineers accountable for quality—an approach that aligns with Boam AI’s emphasis on next-gen AI tools and fast iteration.\\n\\nI’d welcome the chance to partner closely with your CEO, data/engineering/ML teams, and customers to turn customer pull into shipped product across pipelines, schemas, APIs, and integrations.\\n\\nSincerely,\\nLeonid Verman\\n"}	documents/27af6204-a05d-4fc9-8115-a1df26c83ebd/generated/84b74849-4057-4f83-ab89-dd5f2d4ed28f/resume.docx	documents/27af6204-a05d-4fc9-8115-a1df26c83ebd/generated/84b74849-4057-4f83-ab89-dd5f2d4ed28f/resume.pdf	documents/27af6204-a05d-4fc9-8115-a1df26c83ebd/generated/84b74849-4057-4f83-ab89-dd5f2d4ed28f/cover_letter.docx	documents/27af6204-a05d-4fc9-8115-a1df26c83ebd/generated/84b74849-4057-4f83-ab89-dd5f2d4ed28f/cover_letter.pdf	2026-03-18 06:57:31.830465+00
18a9d2d1-b740-4377-a9fd-77129d63d0e3	fe1493e3-80d2-4396-8138-c586c9ecef81	7f75b715-4fd6-4341-ad19-c6431971715e	CARFAX	Senior Software Engineer - Team Lead	{"text": "Oli Treadwell\\nolitreadwell@gmail.com | +64 22 451 9939 (Text first please)\\nlinkedin.com/in/olitreadwell | github.com/olitreadwell | Book a Call\\nSenior Software Engineer\\n\\nSUMMARY\\nSenior Software Engineer with 10+ years of experience building modern web applications with an emphasis on accessible, user-friendly UI and component-driven front-end architecture. Strong React/TypeScript and full-stack delivery (Node.js, Ruby on Rails, PostgreSQL), with a track record of design-system work, testing discipline, and pragmatic technical leadership through code review, delegation, and coaching.\\n\\nSKILLS\\n- Frontend & UX: React, TypeScript, Next.js, Storybook, CSS/SCSS, Design systems, Localisation\\n- Backend & APIs: Node.js, .NET, Ruby on Rails, Python Flask, GraphQL, REST/JSON:API, Schema design\\n- DevOps & Tooling: AWS, Docker, GitHub Actions, CircleCI, Cypress, Jest/React Testing Library (RTL), Monitoring\\n- Leadership & Accessibility: Technical mentoring, Stakeholder facilitation, Accessibility advocacy\\n\\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\\nSenior Software Engineer | Numeral Studio | Wellington, NZ | 2025 – Present\\n- Delivered reusable React/TypeScript components inside Electron with accessible, responsive UI patterns and Jest/React Testing Library coverage, reducing manual errors in compliance reporting workflows.\\n- Built React/TypeScript interfaces and Prisma-backed Node/Express services for HR case workflows, including dynamic staff routing and permissions-focused workflow logic.\\n- Added automated ESLint/Prettier and unit-test checks to support consistent delivery quality across day-to-day feature work.\\n- Supported launch work for the design conference 2025 and 2026 site on Next.js/TypeScript with Sanity CMS and Storybook; extended the design system to reduce duplicate UI code.\\n- Contributed localized feature work for a mobile-first progressive web app marketing demo, collaborating with remote teammates and tuning performance for global launches.\\n- Technologies: React, Next.js, Electron, TypeScript, SCSS, Node.js/Express, Prisma ORM, Sanity CMS, Storybook, GSAP, Cypress, Jest, React Testing Library, GitHub Actions, ESLint, Prettier, localization & accessibility tools.\\n\\nSoftware Engineer (Contract) | PartsTrader Markets Ltd. | Wellington, NZ | 2024 – 2025\\n- Developed a dedicated .NET microservice to interface with a legacy API and built a modern, responsive front-end using React with TypeScript.\\n- Translated Figma designs into dynamic, accessible interfaces using React, TypeScript, and styled-components.\\n- Applied Domain-Driven Design by structuring the service with Repository, Domain Model, Mapper, and Application Service patterns.\\n- Technologies: .NET service layer, React, TypeScript, Cypress, GitHub Actions, domain-driven design patterns.\\n\\nSoftware Engineer & Founder | Habitual Genesis | Remote | 2016 – Present\\n- Partner with authors, museums, and education nonprofits to ship low-maintenance digital products.\\n- Delivered discovery-through-launch engagements while keeping ongoing costs low.\\n- Embedded with stakeholders to clarify needs, prioritize MVPs, and trial marketing ideas without raising spend.\\n- Various projects with General Assembly, Thinkful, Codecademy, and others.\\n- Technologies: JavaScript, HTML5, CSS3, Bootstrap, GitHub, GitHub Pages, Squarespace, Mailchimp, Google Drive.\\n\\nSoftware Engineer & Lead Instructor | The Flatiron School | Remote | 2022 – 2023\\n- Delivered remote and asynchronous technical training on software engineering.\\n- Wrote and presented curriculum covering JavaScript, HTML/CSS, ReactJS, Python, Flask, PostgreSQL, Object-Oriented Programming, CI/CD, Agile, APIs, and Web Accessibility.\\n- Mentored and coached junior engineers, focusing on practical skill development and readiness for day-to-day engineering work.\\n- Led a working group promoting inclusive web design and web accessibility practices.\\n- Technologies: JavaScript, HTML5, CSS3, ReactJS, React Router, Python, Flask, Object-Oriented Programming, CI/CD, Render.com, Agile, APIs, Web Accessibility.\\n\\nSenior Software Engineer | WorkTango (formerly KazooHR) | Remote | 2019 – 2020\\n- Re-architected the Rewards platform UI from Rails-rendered views to ReactJS, resulting in a 15% increase in customer engagement.\\n- Implemented a modular design system to improve UI consistency and support faster, more repeatable UI delivery.\\n- Integrated features across Performance Management and Rewards platforms to overhaul the product suite.\\n- Technologies: ReactJS, Storybook, NodeJS, Jest, Chai, TypeScript, Ruby on Rails, ActiveRecord, RSpec, GraphQL, PostgreSQL, Circle CI, SASS/SCSS, GitHub, Design Language Systems, JIRA, Zeplin, Figma.\\n\\nSoftware Engineer | Condé Nast | Austin, TX | 2017 – 2019\\n- Delivered new design features and ReactJS components for 26+ media brands.\\n- Built and iterated on a brand-agnostic paywall architecture and component suite; achieved a year-over-year increase of 100%+ in monthly subscriptions for Vanity Fair and Wired.\\n- Authored a technology blog post on end-to-end testing of Condé Nast paywalls: https://technology.condenast.com/story/end-to-end-testing-conde-nast-paywalls\\n- Technologies: ReactJS, Storybook, NodeJS, Jest, Puppeteer, TypeScript, SASS, GitHub, Jenkins, CI/CD, Design Language Systems, JIRA.\\n\\nSoftware Engineer & Instructor | Hack Reactor (formerly Galvanize) | Austin, TX | 2016 – 2017\\n- Facilitated technical workshops for full-time and part-time programs in an Agile environment.\\n- Built a mock interview app for students, increasing career services’ capacity to provide feedback.\\n- Technologies: ReactJS, JavaScript, jQuery, Mocha, Chai, HTML, CSS3, SASS/SCSS, PostgreSQL, MySQL, Git, GitHub, Heroku, bash, zsh.\\n\\nSoftware Engineer (Contract) | Bypass Mobile | Austin, TX | 2016 – 2016\\n- Designed and developed a JSON-API spec product licensing platform using Ruby on Rails as part of a small team.\\n- Technologies: JSON-API, Ruby on Rails, ActiveRecord, RSpec, MySQL, Git, GitHub, Vagrant, bash, JIRA.\\n\\nSoftware Engineer | Union Metrics | Austin, TX | 2014 – 2016\\n- Migrated and refactored two legacy codebases to Rails 4, improving maintainability and performance by 20%.\\n- Created a knowledge base of 100 common customer technical challenges, reducing resolution time by 50%.\\n- Technologies: JavaScript, Ruby on Rails, ActiveRecord, RSpec, jQuery, HTML, CSS3, SASS/SCSS, MySQL, Git, GitHub, Vagrant, Jenkins, bash.\\n\\nEDUCATION\\nPostgraduate Diploma in Information Technology | Whitireia and WelTec, New Zealand\\nFull-Stack Web Development, Ruby on Rails, and JavaScript Certification | Dev Bootcamp\\nBS in Business Administration, Entrepreneurship, & International Business | Chapman University\\n\\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\\nFor more details, you can find answers to common hiring questions, my references, and a detailed list of my skills and experience at the following links:\\n- Common Hiring Questions: github.com/olitreadwell/resume/blob/main/common-hiring-questions.md\\n- Portfolio Projects: https://github.com/olitreadwell/resume/blob/main/portfolio-projects.md\\n- Professional References: github.com/olitreadwell/resume/blob/main/linkedin-recommendations.md\\n- Skills and Experience: github.com/olitreadwell/resume/blob/main/skills-and-experience.md\\n", "template_original_filename": "Oli Treadwell - Senior Software Engineer Resume - 2026-03-06.pdf"}	{"text": "Oli Treadwell\\nMarch 18, 2026\\n\\nDear Hiring Manager,\\n\\nI’m applying for the Senior Software Engineer – Team Lead role at CARFAX. I’m a Senior Software Engineer with 10+ years of experience building modern web applications, with a focus on accessible, user-friendly interfaces, component-driven UI architecture, and pragmatic full-stack delivery using React, TypeScript, and Node.js (with additional Ruby on Rails/PostgreSQL experience).\\n\\nAcross product teams, I’ve led and supported front-end modernization and shared UI foundations. At WorkTango, I re-architected a Rewards platform UI from Rails-rendered views to ReactJS and helped implement a modular design system to improve UI consistency across the product. More recently at Numeral Studio, I’ve delivered reusable React/TypeScript components with Jest/React Testing Library coverage and built Node/Express services supporting HR case workflows, while keeping day-to-day delivery quality high via automated linting/formatting and unit-test checks.\\n\\nCARFAX’s Account Engineering mission—delivering a consistent, high-quality customer experience across login, profiles, and shared site experiences—maps well to my strengths in UI architecture, design-system driven reuse, and cross-functional collaboration with design and product. I also bring hands-on mentoring experience (including coaching junior engineers and leading instruction), and I’m comfortable delegating ownership, using code review as a growth tool, and pushing back on risky changes when production stability is at stake.\\n\\nI’d welcome the chance to discuss how I can contribute to CARFAX as a Senior Software Engineer – Team Lead.\\n\\nSincerely,\\nOli Treadwell\\n"}	\N	\N	documents/fe1493e3-80d2-4396-8138-c586c9ecef81/generated/7f75b715-4fd6-4341-ad19-c6431971715e/cover_letter.docx	documents/fe1493e3-80d2-4396-8138-c586c9ecef81/generated/7f75b715-4fd6-4341-ad19-c6431971715e/cover_letter.pdf	2026-03-18 07:26:42.493317+00
