26-03-06.pdf"}	{"text": "Oli Treadwell\\nolitreadwell@gmail.com | linkedin.com/in/olitreadwell | github.com/olitreadwell\\nMarch 18, 2026\\n\\nDear Hiring Manager,\\n\\nI’m writing to apply for the Senior Software Engineer – Team Lead role at CARFAX. I’m a Senior Software Engineer with 10+ years of experience building modern web applications, with deep strength in React and TypeScript UI architecture, component-driven development, and pragmatic full-stack delivery with Node.js and Ruby on Rails.\\n\\nAcross product teams, I’ve focused on creating consistent, high-quality front-end experiences through reusable components and design-system practices. At WorkTango, I re-architected the Rewards platform UI from Rails to ReactJS and implemented a modular design system to improve UI consistency; this work is also where I partnered closely with design and engineering to ship customer-facing improvements. In my current role at Numeral Studio, I’ve continued that approach by delivering accessible React/TypeScript components (including Electron UI) with Jest/React Testing Library coverage, and by extending a Storybook-backed design system on a Next.js/TypeScript site.\\n\\nAs a team lead, I bring hands-on mentorship and an ownership mindset: delegating meaningful work, using code review to raise quality, and coaching engineers on testing and maintainable component boundaries. I also have experience collaborating in distributed and cross-functional environments with Product, UX, and other stakeholders, translating designs from tools like Figma/Zeplin into accessible, responsive interfaces.\\n\\nCARFAX’s focus on building secure, consistent customer experiences and a strong engineering culture is a fit for how I like to work: high standards, continuous improvement, and practical delivery. I’d welcome the opportunity to discuss how my React/TypeScript architecture experience and mentoring style can support the Account Engineering team.\\n\\nSincerely,\\nOli Treadwell\\n"}	docume